Spring Data JPA parses your repository method names and generates JPQL queries automatically:

```java
public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {
    List<User> findByLastName(String lastName);
    // → SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.lastName = ?1

    Optional<User> findByEmail(String email);
    // → SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = ?1

    List<User> findByAgeGreaterThan(int age);
    // → SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.age > ?1
}
```

Spring Data parses the method name at application startup and creates the query implementation.

```java
// JPQL with named parameter
@Query("SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.email = :email")
Optional<User> findByEmailCustom(@Param("email") String email);

// JPQL with positional parameter
@Query("SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.status = ?1 AND u.age > ?2")
List<User> findActiveUsersOlderThan(String status, int age);

// Native SQL
@Query(value = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE created_at > :date", nativeQuery = true)
List<User> findRecentUsers(@Param("date") LocalDate date);

// Modifying query (UPDATE/DELETE)
@Modifying
@Transactional
@Query("UPDATE User u SET u.status = :status WHERE u.id = :id")
int updateStatus(@Param("id") Long id, @Param("status") String status);
```

```java
// Contains — LIKE '%text%'
List<User> findByNameContaining(String text);
List<User> findByNameContainingIgnoreCase(String text); // case-insensitive

// Starts with — LIKE 'prefix%'
List<User> findByNameStartingWith(String prefix);

// Ends with — LIKE '%suffix'
List<User> findByNameEndingWith(String suffix);

// Like — you provide the % wildcards
List<User> findByNameLike(String pattern);
// Usage: findByNameLike("%alice%") — equivalent to Containing
```

```java
// IN clause
List<User> findByStatusIn(List<String> statuses);
// → WHERE status IN ('ACTIVE', 'PENDING')

List<User> findByIdIn(List<Long> ids);
// → WHERE id IN (1, 2, 3)

// NOT IN
List<User> findByStatusNotIn(List<String> statuses);

// BETWEEN
List<User> findByAgeBetween(int minAge, int maxAge);
// → WHERE age BETWEEN 18 AND 65

List<User> findByCreatedAtBetween(LocalDateTime start, LocalDateTime end);
// → WHERE created_at BETWEEN ? AND ?
```

```java
// Top N results — newest first
List<User> findTop5ByOrderByCreatedAtDesc();
// → SELECT ... ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 5

// With condition
List<User> findTop3ByStatusOrderByCreatedAtDesc(String status);

// Single result — first match
Optional<User> findFirstByEmailOrderByCreatedAtDesc(String email);

// Top by some ranking field
Optional<Product> findTopByOrderByPriceDesc(); // most expensive
```

**Derived method** — clean and readable:
```java
List<User> findByStatusAndAgeGreaterThan(String status, int age);
```

**@Query** — when method name gets ridiculous:
```java
// BAD derived method:
List<User> findByFirstNameAndLastNameAndStatusAndAgeGreaterThanAndEmailNotNull(...);

// GOOD @Query:
@Query("SELECT u FROM User u WHERE u.firstName=:fn AND u.lastName=:ln " +
       "AND u.status=:s AND u.age > :age AND u.email IS NOT NULL")
List<User> findEligibleUsers(@Param("fn") String fn, ...);
```
